From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: a queue depth of 8 on hosts without command queueing

Each request the block layer pre-allocates for an MMC queue carries its own
scatterlist (max_segs entries: 2 KiB on the X1000's controller), for the
hardware queue (64 tags) and again for the I/O scheduler's (2 x 64 = 128):
386 KiB of kernel memory that never goes back, on a player with 24 MiB. A
plain SD card takes one request at a time; 8 in flight (16 for the
scheduler, which still merges and sorts) keep it busy. 48 KiB instead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific memory trade-off]

--- a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@
 }
 
 /* Set queue depth to get a reasonable value for q->nr_requests */
-#define MMC_QUEUE_DEPTH 64
+#define MMC_QUEUE_DEPTH 8
 
 /**
  * mmc_init_queue - initialise a queue structure.
